NeoDEM TASK-223 -- one sim boot, three answers.

Applies on top of 0001-neodem-g1-wholebody-sim.patch and the Isaac Lab 3.0 port
already present in the checkout working tree. Three hunks:

  1. action_provider_wh_dds.py: obs_scales. Upstream ships all 1.0; the ONNX
     policy carries no normalisation of its own, so the scales here are the only
     normalisation the policy ever sees. Defaults to Unitree's locomotion values
     (ang_vel 0.25, joint_vel 0.05); set NEODEM_OBS_SCALES=upstream to get the
     shipped all-1.0 behaviour back without re-patching.
  2. action_provider_wh_dds.py: _task223_log -- lead 3, from inside the sim, free.
     Prints projected_gravity_b (a convention-free uprightness test that no
     quaternion-order bug can reach), the root height, the true roll/pitch from
     root_quat_w read as (x,y,z,w), the leg joint angles against their defaults,
     and -- once, at step 0, before the first action is applied -- the full
     articulation joint-name order.
  3. g1_29dof_state.py: the IMU quaternion published to rt/lowstate. Upstream's
     assume_w_first=True was right on Isaac Lab 2.x and is wrong on 3.0, where
     the quaternion is (x,y,z,w). Combined with dds/g1_robot_dds.py:101 it made a
     perfectly upright base publish as |roll| = pi, so isaac_gait_probe.py's
     "base upright" check could never pass, on any hypothesis.

